---

<DocsLayout
  title="Plugins"
  subtitle="How nikcli installs plugins, patches server/TUI config, loads built-ins, and exposes plugin hooks."
  description="Guide to Nikcli plugins, installation, built-in hooks, server/TUI patching, and plugin configuration."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="overview" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Plugins extend server-side agent behavior and TUI behavior. Server plugin loading is in
      <code>packages/nikcli/src/plugin/index.ts</code>. Plugin installation and config patching are
      in <code>packages/nikcli/src/plugin/install.ts</code>. TUI plugin runtime lives under
      <code>packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd/tui/plugin</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-8">
      <DocCard title="Server hooks" eyebrow="Runtime">
        <p>Provider auth, tool hooks, event hooks, notifications, and session behavior load in the server plugin service.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="TUI hooks" eyebrow="UI">
        <p>TUI plugins can register commands, routes, dialogs, keybinds, and sidebar features.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Installer" eyebrow="CLI">
        <p><code>nikcli plugin</code> installs a package, reads its manifest, and patches local or global config.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Built-ins" eyebrow="Default">
        <p>Internal auth and notification plugins always load; external built-ins load unless disabled.</p>
      </DocCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="install" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Install a plugin</h2>
    <DocCode language="bash">
nikcli plugin @scope/my-plugin
nikcli plugin @scope/my-plugin --global
nikcli plugin @scope/my-plugin@1.2.3 --force
    </DocCode>
    <p>The install task performs four steps:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Resolve and install the package target.</li>
      <li>Read plugin metadata from <code>package.json</code>.</li>
      <li>Detect server and/or TUI targets from manifest or exports.</li>
      <li>Patch <code>nikcli.json</code> and/or <code>tui.json</code> in the selected scope.</li>
    </ol>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>--global</code></td><td>Patch global config under <code>Global.Path.config</code> instead of project config.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--force</code></td><td>Replace an existing plugin entry for the same package.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>version suffix</td><td>Installer preserves the requested package spec and version.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="patching" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Config patching</h2>
    <p>
      <code>patchPluginConfig</code> uses <code>jsonc-parser</code> edits instead of string hacks.
      It can patch server config <code>plugin</code> and TUI config depending on detected targets.
      Duplicate detection compares package names, not only the full versioned spec.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>When used</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>add</code></td><td>No existing plugin entry for the package.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>noop</code></td><td>Same plugin spec is already configured and force is false.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>replace</code></td><td>Existing package entry differs and <code>--force</code> is set.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCode language="json" title="server plugin config">
&#123;
  "plugin": [
    "@scope/my-plugin"
  ]
&#125;
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="server-runtime" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Server runtime</h2>
    <p>
      Server plugin loading starts with internal plugins that are imported directly. Then configured
      plugins plus external built-ins are loaded. If a plugin path is not <code>file://</code>, nikcli
      installs the package before importing it.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Build plugin input, including SDK client and runtime helpers.</li>
      <li>Load internal auth/notification plugins.</li>
      <li>Copy configured plugin specifiers from config.</li>
      <li>Add external built-ins unless <code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_DEFAULT_PLUGINS</code> is set.</li>
      <li>Ignore old Codex/Copilot auth plugin specs that are now first-party.</li>
      <li>Install and import package specifiers.</li>
      <li>Load v1 <code>server</code> export when present, otherwise invoke exported plugin functions.</li>
      <li>Deduplicate duplicate function references from named and default exports.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="tui-runtime" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>TUI runtime</h2>
    <p>
      TUI plugin APIs are built in <code>cli/cmd/tui/plugin/api.tsx</code> and loaded by
      <code>plugin/runtime.ts</code>. Plugins can add routes, commands, dialogs, keybinds, and UI
      surfaces while the TUI app is running.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>API area</th><th>Capability</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Route</td><td>Navigate home, session, changes, tree, graph, GitHub, or plugin routes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Command</td><td>Register command palette entries and key-triggered commands.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Dialog</td><td>Open, clear, size, and inspect dialog stack.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Keybind</td><td>Match, print, and create plugin keybind definitions.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Slots/features</td><td>Register sidebar or system plugin manager UI where supported.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="built-ins" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Built-in plugins</h2>
    <p>
      Internal built-ins are directly imported and do not depend on package installation. They include
      Codex auth, GitHub Copilot auth, xAI auth, Cursor auth, Cloudflare Workers/Gateway auth, and
      the notification plugin. External built-ins are appended from the built-in list unless disabled.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Built-in</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Codex auth</td><td>First-party Codex authentication support.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>GitHub Copilot auth</td><td>Copilot and enterprise provider auth.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>xAI auth</td><td>xAI provider auth integration.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cursor auth</td><td>Cursor ACP/provider auth integration.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cloudflare auth</td><td>Cloudflare Workers and AI Gateway auth flows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Notify plugin</td><td>Session idle/error, permission, question, Slack, Discord, and macOS notifications.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCode language="bash">
NIKCLI_DISABLE_DEFAULT_PLUGINS=1 nikcli
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="manifest" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Plugin manifest</h2>
    <p>
      The installer reads package metadata with <code>readPluginPackage</code>. Target detection
      accepts explicit plugin target metadata and also detects packages that expose
      <code>./server</code> and/or <code>./tui</code> exports. A package with only <code>main</code>
      or string <code>exports</code> is treated as a server plugin.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="package.json">
&#123;
  "name": "@scope/my-plugin",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "exports": &#123;
    "./server": "./dist/server.js",
    "./tui": "./dist/tui.js"
  &#125;,
  "oc-plugin": ["server", "tui"]
&#125;
    </DocCode>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Tuple targets">
      <p>
        Target entries may also be tuples with target options, such as a TUI target plus plugin
        options. The patcher preserves target options when adding config.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="skills" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <p>
      Skills are related but not the same as plugins. Skills are prompt/context assets discovered by
      <code>skill/skill.ts</code>. The skill glob scans <code>skill/**/SKILL.md</code> and
      <code>skills/**/SKILL.md</code> under config directories, plus external sources unless disabled.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Plugin</th><th>Skill</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Runtime code</td><td>Yes, imported and executed.</td><td>No, prompt/context instructions and assets.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Config field</td><td><code>plugin</code></td><td>Discovered from directories and external skill locations.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>TUI manager</td><td>System plugin manager and plugin APIs.</td><td>Skills dialog and skill install/search UI.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Disable flag</td><td><code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_DEFAULT_PLUGINS</code> for default external plugins.</td><td><code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_EXTERNAL_SKILLS</code> for external skills.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="notifications" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Notifications</h2>
    <p>
      Notifications are implemented as an internal plugin created by <code>createNotifyPlugin</code>.
      It reads <code>notifications.notify</code> and <code>notifications.todo</code>, applies rate
      limits, retry/backoff, circuit breaker behavior, quiet hours, and connector-backed Slack or
      Discord delivery.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="notify config">
&#123;
  "notifications": &#123;
    "notify": &#123;
      "enabled": true,
      "events": &#123;
        "sessionIdle": true,
        "sessionError": true,
        "permissionAsked": true,
        "questionAsked": true
      &#125;,
      "slack": &#123; "enabled": true, "connector": "slack", "channel": "#builds" &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="failure-modes" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Failure modes</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Install failed</td><td>Package resolution, registry auth, or unavailable version.</td><td>Check the error detail from <code>Process.RunFailedError</code> and npm registry settings.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>No plugin targets found</td><td>Package lacks recognized manifest targets and exports.</td><td>Add <code>oc-plugin</code>, <code>./server</code>, <code>./tui</code>, <code>main</code>, or string exports.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Invalid JSON while patching</td><td>Target config file is not valid JSONC.</td><td>Fix reported line/column and rerun install.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plugin loads twice</td><td>Package exports same function as named and default export.</td><td>Runtime deduplicates identical function references; check distinct functions if duplicates remain.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Built-in plugin install fails</td><td>External built-in package could not be installed.</td><td>Server publishes a session error and continues without that built-in.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>TUI plugin route missing</td><td>Plugin route id was not registered or runtime disposed.</td><td>Check TUI plugin runtime status and route registration.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="source-anchors" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Source anchors</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>File</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Server plugin runtime</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/plugin/index.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plugin install and patching</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/plugin/install.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plugin package parsing</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/plugin/shared.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>CLI command</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd/plug.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>TUI plugin API</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd/tui/plugin/api.tsx</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>TUI plugin runtime</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd/tui/plugin/runtime.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>System plugin manager</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/cli/cmd/tui/feature-plugins/system</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plugin contracts package</td><td><code>packages/plugin</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Skills</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/skill/skill.ts</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
